      <main id="content"><h1>StandardizedRGOPositionFisher: mathematical reading route</h1><p>Read the statements and derivations in source order. Every result has its own optional Lean statement and proof. Source assumptions, library reuse and unproved boundaries are kept explicit.</p><ol><li><a href="#decl-autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-standardizedrgopositio-ff78a6f59e">Actual standardized RGO position and Fisher</a></li></ol><section id="decl-autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-standardizedrgopositio-ff78a6f59e"><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h2>Actual standardized RGO position and Fisher</h2><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher</code> · theorem · <a href="index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h3>Mathematical statement</h3><p class="reader-claim">Produce one measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. For literal rho(u)=V(p+sqrteta*u)-V(p)-sqrteta*inner(gradientV(p),u) and Q=normu^2/2+rho, produce C2, mode0, 0&lt;=Hessrho&lt;=etaI and I&lt;=HessQ&lt;=(1+eta)I. The actual RGO R=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)) is a probability measure, and its actual standardized pushforward r equals volume.tilted(-Q). Genuine position and rho-gradient L2 satisfy integral normu^2 dr&lt;=d and integral normgradrho^2 dr&lt;=eta^2 integral normu^2 dr&lt;=eta^2 d. Only the last TWO comparisons of(4.6) are covered; the first W2 comparison is open.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[r=(x\mapsto (x-p)/\sqrt\eta)_\#R=Z_Q^{-1}e^{-Q(u)}du,\quad\int\|\nabla\rho\|^2dr\le\eta^2\int\|u\|^2dr\le\eta^2d.\]</div><h4>Proof roadmap</h4><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Produce the true proximal point and base law</strong><p>Positive source curvature yields exp(-V) integrability and a probability mu. Reuse the actual full-range measurable proximal producer, preserving p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. There is no selector or probability premise.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Differentiate the literal standardized potential</strong><p>Apply genuine affine chain rules and the real Hilbert Riesz gradient to the literal rho and Q. The linear term cancels the gradient at zero; the quadratic term contributes the identity Hessian.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Derive actual curvature and the mode</strong><p>Retained source curvature and positive eta give 0&lt;=Hessrho&lt;=etaI and I&lt;=HessQ&lt;=(1+eta)I, with both real gradients zero at zero. C2 is produced from V; none of these estimates is supplied.</p></li><li><span>4</span><strong>Produce genuine Q normalization and the position moment</strong><p>Apply the accepted noncompact Gibbs position-moment producer to the actual Q with alpha1,beta1+eta and mode0. Its actual weighted IBP proves the required ordinary-volume L1 product integrability and applies full-space Fubini/IBP, without a cutoff assumption or construction, yielding positive partition, probability and positionL2. The current source theorem assumes no IBP or moment certificate.</p></li><li><span>5</span><strong>Identify the literal true RGO law</strong><p>Combine the actual two tilts into W=V+norm(x-y)^2/(2eta). Exact proximal optimality gives W(p+sqrteta*u)=Q(u)+C, with C=V(p)+norm(p-y)^2/(2eta). Apply canonical affine transport, then cancel C using the internally produced Q probability and integrability. The true RGO weight is bounded by1 under probability mu, so R is independently a probability measure.</p></li><li><span>6</span><strong>Prove the pointwise gradient comparison</strong><p>The actual C2 curvature theorem supplies eta-Lipschitz gradientrho. Its mode0 gives normgradrho(u)&lt;=eta*normu; squaring keeps exactly eta^2. This is a real derivative estimate, not a gradient-output law certificate.</p></li><li><span>7</span><strong>Integrate under the actual standardized posterior</strong><p>Domination by the genuine position-square integrable function proves rho-gradient L2. Integral monotonicity and the genuine dimension bound give the last TWO comparisons of4.6 in squared form. No Talagrand/LSI/W2 estimate follows without its separate dependency.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h4>All objects and hypotheses</h4><ul><li>Source beta=1, alpha=kappa^-1, real kappa&gt;=1; actual C2 V with kappa^-1*normv^2&lt;=D2V(x)[v,v]&lt;=normv^2 for every x,v.</li><li>Finite real complete Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero, and arbitrary measurable parameter space S; measurable eta/y with every0&lt;eta(s)&lt;=1. These coordinate-free and parameter-space extensions are disclosed.</li><li>No supplied proximal point, law identity, normalizer, probability, curvature, gradient or moment certificate. Actual p, mu/R/r probability, normalized affine law, C2 curvature/mode and genuine position/Fisher L2 are internally produced. The numerical-prox eta&lt;=1/(2beta) cap is a separate computational contract.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h3>Mathematical proof</h3><div class="proof-reader-step"><h5>1. Produce the true proximal point and base law</h5><p>Positive source curvature yields exp(-V) integrability and a probability mu. Reuse the actual full-range measurable proximal producer, preserving p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. There is no selector or probability premise.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\mu=Z_V^{-1}e^{-V}dx,\quad p_s+\eta_s\nabla V(p_s)=y_s.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>StrongConvexGibbsIntegrability.integrable_exp_neg_of_strongConvexOn; HessianStrongConvexity; FullRangeProximalGaussianOracle</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h5>2. Differentiate the literal standardized potential</h5><p>Apply genuine affine chain rules and the real Hilbert Riesz gradient to the literal rho and Q. The linear term cancels the gradient at zero; the quadratic term contributes the identity Hessian.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\nabla\rho(u)=\sqrt\eta[\nabla V(p+\sqrt\eta u)-\nabla V(p)],\quad D^2\rho=\eta D^2V,\quad D^2Q=I+\eta D^2V.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>actual_standardized_calculus; HasFDerivAt.comp; inner_gradient_left; HasFDerivAt.norm_sq</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h5>3. Derive actual curvature and the mode</h5><p>Retained source curvature and positive eta give 0&lt;=Hessrho&lt;=etaI and I&lt;=HessQ&lt;=(1+eta)I, with both real gradients zero at zero. C2 is produced from V; none of these estimates is supplied.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\nabla\rho(0)=\nabla Q(0)=0,\quad 0\preceq D^2\rho\preceq\eta I,\quad I\preceq D^2Q\preceq(1+\eta)I.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>actual_standardized_calculus; hH; mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h5>4. Produce genuine Q normalization and the position moment</h5><p>Apply the accepted noncompact Gibbs position-moment producer to the actual Q with alpha1,beta1+eta and mode0. Its actual weighted IBP proves the required ordinary-volume L1 product integrability and applies full-space Fubini/IBP, without a cutoff assumption or construction, yielding positive partition, probability and positionL2. The current source theorem assumes no IBP or moment certificate.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\int\langle u,\nabla Q(u)\rangle dr=d,\quad\int\|u\|^2dr\le d.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>GibbsPositionMoment.gibbs_position_moment; memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h5>5. Identify the literal true RGO law</h5><p>Combine the actual two tilts into W=V+norm(x-y)^2/(2eta). Exact proximal optimality gives W(p+sqrteta*u)=Q(u)+C, with C=V(p)+norm(p-y)^2/(2eta). Apply canonical affine transport, then cancel C using the internally produced Q probability and integrability. The true RGO weight is bounded by1 under probability mu, so R is independently a probability measure.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[W(p+\sqrt\eta u)=Q(u)+C,\quad r=(x\mapsto(x-p)/\sqrt\eta)_\#R=Z_Q^{-1}e^{-Q}du.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>actual_standardized_law; AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs; tilted_tilted; tilted_const; isProbabilityMeasure_tilted</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h5>6. Prove the pointwise gradient comparison</h5><p>The actual C2 curvature theorem supplies eta-Lipschitz gradientrho. Its mode0 gives normgradrho(u)&lt;=eta*normu; squaring keeps exactly eta^2. This is a real derivative estimate, not a gradient-output law certificate.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\|\nabla\rho(u)\|^2\le\eta^2\|u\|^2.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic; LipschitzWith.norm_sub_le</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h5>7. Integrate under the actual standardized posterior</h5><p>Domination by the genuine position-square integrable function proves rho-gradient L2. Integral monotonicity and the genuine dimension bound give the last TWO comparisons of4.6 in squared form. No Talagrand/LSI/W2 estimate follows without its separate dependency.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\int\|\nabla\rho\|^2dr\le\eta^2\int\|u\|^2dr\le\eta^2d.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>Integrable.mono&#x27;; integral_mono; integral_const_mul; memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h3>Lean verification</h3><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher"><summary>Lean statement · standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher</summary><p>Produce one measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. For literal rho(u)=V(p+sqrteta*u)-V(p)-sqrteta*inner(gradientV(p),u) and Q=normu^2/2+rho, produce C2, mode0, 0&lt;=Hessrho&lt;=etaI and I&lt;=HessQ&lt;=(1+eta)I. The actual RGO R=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)) is a probability measure, and its actual standardized pushforward r equals volume.tilted(-Q). Genuine position and rho-gradient L2 satisfy integral normu^2 dr&lt;=d and integral normgradrho^2 dr&lt;=eta^2 integral normu^2 dr&lt;=eta^2 d. Only the last TWO comparisons of(4.6) are covered; the first W2 comparison is open.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher
    {E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}
    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)
    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)
    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)
    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 &lt; eta s) (hsmall : ∀ s, eta s ≤ 1) :
    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧
      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧
      let rho := fun s u =&gt; V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-
        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u
      let Q := fun s u =&gt; ‖u‖^2/2+rho s u
      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -V x)
      let R := fun s =&gt; mu.tilted (fun x =&gt; -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))
      let r := fun s =&gt; (R s).map (fun x =&gt; (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))
      IsProbabilityMeasure mu ∧
        ∀ s, IsProbabilityMeasure (R s) ∧
          ContDiff ℝ 2 (rho s) ∧ ContDiff ℝ 2 (Q s) ∧
          gradient (rho s) 0=0 ∧ gradient (Q s) 0=0 ∧
          (∀ u v : E, 0 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ∧
            fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ≤ eta s*‖v‖^2) ∧
          (∀ u v : E, ‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ∧
            fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ≤ (1+eta s)*‖v‖^2) ∧
          r s=(volume : Measure E).tilted (fun u =&gt; -Q s u) ∧
          IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) ∧ MemLp id 2 (r s) ∧
          Integrable (fun u =&gt; ‖u‖^2) (r s) ∧
          (∫ u, ‖u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E ∧
          MemLp (gradient (rho s)) 2 (r s) ∧
          (∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤
            (eta s)^2*(∫ u, ‖u‖^2 ∂r s) ∧
          (∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤
            (eta s)^2*Module.finrank ℝ E</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-standardizedrgopositionfisher.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher"><summary>Lean proof · standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher</summary><p>Produce the true proximal point and base law; Differentiate the literal standardized potential; Derive actual curvature and the mode; Produce genuine Q normalization and the position moment; Identify the literal true RGO law; Prove the pointwise gradient comparison; Integrate under the actual standardized posterior</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher
    {E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}
    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)
    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)
    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)
    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 &lt; eta s) (hsmall : ∀ s, eta s ≤ 1) :
    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧
      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧
      let rho := fun s u =&gt; V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-
        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u
      let Q := fun s u =&gt; ‖u‖^2/2+rho s u
      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -V x)
      let R := fun s =&gt; mu.tilted (fun x =&gt; -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))
      let r := fun s =&gt; (R s).map (fun x =&gt; (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))
      IsProbabilityMeasure mu ∧
        ∀ s, IsProbabilityMeasure (R s) ∧
          ContDiff ℝ 2 (rho s) ∧ ContDiff ℝ 2 (Q s) ∧
          gradient (rho s) 0=0 ∧ gradient (Q s) 0=0 ∧
          (∀ u v : E, 0 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ∧
            fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ≤ eta s*‖v‖^2) ∧
          (∀ u v : E, ‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ∧
            fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ≤ (1+eta s)*‖v‖^2) ∧
          r s=(volume : Measure E).tilted (fun u =&gt; -Q s u) ∧
          IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) ∧ MemLp id 2 (r s) ∧
          Integrable (fun u =&gt; ‖u‖^2) (r s) ∧
          (∫ u, ‖u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E ∧
          MemLp (gradient (rho s)) 2 (r s) ∧
          (∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤
            (eta s)^2*(∫ u, ‖u‖^2 ∂r s) ∧
          (∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤
            (eta s)^2*Module.finrank ℝ E := by
  have ha : 0&lt;κ⁻¹ := inv_pos.mpr (lt_of_lt_of_le zero_lt_one hκ)
  have hiV := AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.StrongConvexGibbsIntegrability.integrable_exp_neg_of_strongConvexOn
    ha (hV.differentiable (by norm_num))
    (AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.HessianStrongConvexity.strongConvexOn_univ_of_fderiv2_lower hV (fun x v =&gt; (hH x v).1))
  let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -V x)
  have hmu : IsProbabilityMeasure mu := isProbabilityMeasure_tilted hiV
  have : IsProbabilityMeasure mu := hmu
  obtain ⟨p,hpm,heq,_hrest⟩ := FullRangeProximalGaussianOracle.full_range_proximal_gaussian_oracle
    hκ hV hH heta hy hpos hsmall
  let rho := fun s u =&gt; V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-
    Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u
  let Q := fun s u =&gt; ‖u‖^2/2+rho s u
  let R := fun s =&gt; mu.tilted (fun x =&gt; -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))
  let r := fun s =&gt; (R s).map (fun x =&gt; (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))
  refine ⟨p,hpm,heq,?_⟩
  change IsProbabilityMeasure mu ∧ _
  refine ⟨hmu,?_⟩
  intro s
  have hη : 0&lt;eta s := hpos s
  obtain ⟨hρ,hQ,hρ0,hQ0,hρdd,hQdd⟩ := actual_standardized_calculus hV (p s) (hpos s)
  have hrhoH : ∀ u v : E, 0 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ≤ eta s*‖v‖^2 := by
    intro u v
    rw [hρdd]
    constructor
    · exact mul_nonneg (hpos s).le ((mul_nonneg ha.le (sq_nonneg ‖v‖)).trans (hH _ v).1)
    · exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hH _ v).2 (hpos s).le
  have hQH : ∀ u v : E, ‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ≤ (1+eta s)*‖v‖^2 := by
    intro u v
    rw [hQdd]
    constructor
    · exact le_add_of_nonneg_right (mul_nonneg (hpos s).le ((mul_nonneg ha.le (sq_nonneg ‖v‖)).trans (hH _ v).1))
    · nlinarith [mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hH (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u) v).2 (hpos s).le]
  let beta : ℝ≥0 := ⟨1+eta s,by positivity⟩
  have hβ : (1:ℝ≥0)≤beta := by change 1≤1+eta s; linarith [hpos s]
  have hHQ : ∀ u v : E, ((1:ℝ≥0):ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ≤ (beta:ℝ)*‖v‖^2 := by
    change ∀ u v : E, 1*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ≤ (1+eta s)*‖v‖^2
    simpa only [one_mul] using hQH
  obtain ⟨hqp,hiq,_hqpos,hip,_hpair,_heqd,hbd⟩ :=
    GibbsPositionMoment.gibbs_position_moment (by norm_num : (0:ℝ≥0)&lt;1) hβ hQ hHQ (0:E) hQ0
  have hlaw : r s=(volume : Measure E).tilted (fun u =&gt; -Q s u) :=
    actual_standardized_law V (hpos s) (p s) (y s) (heq s) hiV hiq hqp
  have hpr : IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) := hlaw.symm ▸ hqp
  have hipos : Integrable (fun u =&gt; ‖u‖^2) (r s) := by
    rw [hlaw]
    simpa only [sub_zero] using hip
  have hbound : (∫ u, ‖u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E := by
    rw [hlaw]
    simpa only [sub_zero,NNReal.coe_one,div_one] using hbd
  have hlp : MemLp id 2 (r s) :=
    (memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm (by fun_prop)).mpr hipos
  let b : ℝ≥0 := ⟨eta s,(hpos s).le⟩
  have hHρ : ∀ u v : E, ((0:ℝ≥0):ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ≤ (b:ℝ)*‖v‖^2 := by
    change ∀ u v : E, 0*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ≤ eta s*‖v‖^2
    simpa only [zero_mul] using hrhoH
  have hlip : LipschitzWith b (gradient (rho s)) := by
    simpa only [NNReal.coe_zero,zero_div,zero_mul,add_zero] using (AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic
      (r:=0) hρ hHρ (0:E)).2
  have hpoint (u : E) : ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ≤ (eta s)^2*‖u‖^2 := by
    have h := hlip.norm_sub_le u 0
    rw [hρ0,sub_zero,sub_zero] at h
    have hs := (sq_le_sq₀ (norm_nonneg _) (mul_nonneg (hpos s).le (norm_nonneg u))).mpr h
    simpa only [mul_pow] using hs
  have hgcont : Continuous (gradient (rho s)) := hlip.continuous
  have hif : Integrable (fun u =&gt; ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2) (r s) := by
    apply (hipos.const_mul ((eta s)^2)).mono&#x27; (by fun_prop)
    filter_upwards with u
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs,abs_of_nonneg (sq_nonneg _)]
    exact hpoint u
  have hlf : MemLp (gradient (rho s)) 2 (r s) :=
    (memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm hgcont.aestronglyMeasurable).mpr hif
  have hfp : (∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤
      (eta s)^2*(∫ u, ‖u‖^2 ∂r s) := by
    rw [← integral_const_mul]
    exact integral_mono hif (hipos.const_mul ((eta s)^2)) hpoint
  have hfd : (∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤ (eta s)^2*Module.finrank ℝ E :=
    hfp.trans (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hbound (sq_nonneg _))
  have hiR : Integrable (fun x =&gt; Real.exp (-‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))) mu := by
    apply (integrable_const (1:ℝ)).mono&#x27; (by fun_prop)
    filter_upwards with x
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs,abs_of_nonneg (Real.exp_pos _).le]
    apply Real.exp_le_one_iff.mpr
    exact div_nonpos_of_nonpos_of_nonneg (neg_nonpos.mpr (sq_nonneg _)) (by positivity)
  have hRp : IsProbabilityMeasure (R s) := isProbabilityMeasure_tilted hiR
  exact ⟨hRp,hρ,hQ,hρ0,hQ0,hrhoH,hQH,hlaw,hpr,hlp,hipos,hbound,hlf,hfp,hfd⟩

end
end AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOPositionFisher</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-standardizedrgopositionfisher.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><details class="reader-ledger boundary-ledger"><summary>Scope and omitted-condition boundaries</summary><ul><li>Source realκ&gt;=1,beta1/alphakappainv,C2/globalbothcurvature and every0&lt;eta&lt;=1 retained. Fullfinite real Hilbert/Borel incl0 and arbitrary measurableS are disclosed extensions. Actualp,normalizedmu/R/r,affinelaw,curvature/stationarity andtrue moments are all outputs, never certificates. Generic canonical affine transport needs only nonzero scale and proves identity of Mathlib normalized tilts; it does not assert a probability law without produced positive integrability. GaussianTalagrand/LSI/FIRSTW2 inequality4.6,bias4.2/MGF4.3/fullLemma4.2,higher/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization,posteriorjointMarkovsemantics,actualsamplers/PBPSreflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation,main/work/composition OPEN. Actualr/R distinct from Gaussiangradientoutput and HMC K/Khat/Kbar. Numericalprox sourcecapeta&lt;=1/(2beta) remains; TV never transfers unboundedcost.</li></ul></details><details class="proof-reader-provenance reader-ledger"><summary>Sources, dependencies, and reuse</summary><h3>Source and reuse</h3><h4>Samplinglib parents called</h4><ul><li><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-fullrangeproximalgaussianoracle.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-fullrangeproximalgauss-466257d4a8"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.FullRangeProximalGaussianOracle.full_range_proximal_gaussian_oracle</code></a></li><li><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-gibbspositionmoment.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-gibbspositionmoment-g